args: opentide --json setup --help
exit: 0

━━━ stdout
Set up a detection repository and its tooling

Usage: opentide setup [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  repo       Scaffold a detection repository
  platforms  Enable platform configuration files
  ci         Write CI/CD pipeline files
  env        Write .env.example and ignore .env
  hooks      Validate objects on every commit
  mcp        Write MCP configuration for editors and agents
  vscode     Write VS Code schemas and snippets (deprecated)
  skills     Discover and install agent skills

Options:
  -C, --path <PATH>
          Repository path
          
          [default: .]

      --name <NAME>
          Repository name, used in the README

      --org <ORG>
          Organisation or team, used in the README

      --description <DESCRIPTION>
          One-line description, used in the README

      --platform <PLATFORM>
          Enable a detection platform (repeatable): sentinel, defender_for_endpoint, splunk, sentinel_one, crowdstrike, harfanglab, carbon_black_cloud, elastic, sysdig, bitdefender, graylog, exabeam, google_secops
          
          [possible values: sentinel, defender_for_endpoint, splunk, sentinel_one, crowdstrike, harfanglab, carbon_black_cloud, elastic, sysdig, bitdefender, graylog, exabeam, google_secops]

      --ci <PROVIDER>
          CI/CD pipeline to write: github, gitlab, azure or none
          
          [possible values: github, gitlab, azure, none]

      --staging, --no-staging
          Deploy to staging tenants from pull requests
          
          [default: staging]

      --inflight, --no-inflight
          Update .opentide/inflight/ preview shards on pull requests
          
          [default: inflight]

      --sharing, --no-sharing
          Share changed objects on the default branch (off unless selected)
          
          [default: no-sharing]

      --lint-changed, --lint-all
          Gate lint on the object files each run changes, so a catalogue with inherited findings can adopt it (validate still checks every file)
          
          [default: lint-all]

      --promotion, --no-promotion
          Write [promotion] enabled in deployment.toml. Omit to keep the repository's setting.

      --promotion-target <PROMOTION_TARGET>
          Status deploy promotes rules to. Omit to keep the repository's setting.

      --python-version <PYTHON_VERSION>
          Python version the pipeline installs
          
          [default: 3.12]

      --explorer-pages, --no-explorer-pages
          Include GitHub Pages explorer build and deploy jobs
          
          [default: no-explorer-pages]

      --variable-group <NAME>
          Azure Pipelines: link this Library variable group in variables: (repeatable; ignored with a warning for github and gitlab)

      --default-branch <DEFAULT_BRANCH>
          Branch that deploys and receives inflight shards (default: origin/HEAD, then the checked-out branch, then init.defaultBranch, then main; GitLab uses $CI_DEFAULT_BRANCH)

      --vscode-setup
          Run deprecated setup vscode: the extension recommendation and snippets

      --mcp <HOST>
          Write MCP configuration for vscode, cursor, claude-code or generic (repeatable)
          
          [possible values: vscode, cursor, claude-code, generic]

      --skills <TARGET>
          Install agent skills for claude-code, cursor, github-copilot or generic (repeatable)
          
          [possible values: cursor, claude-code, generic, github-copilot]

      --plugin
          Register the opentidehq/skills Agent Plugin for Claude Code (.claude/settings.json)

      --hooks
          Validate objects on every commit

      --env
          Write .env.example and ignore .env

      --plan
          List the files each step would write, and write nothing

  -y, --yes
          Non-interactive mode

      --help
          Print help

Examples:
  $ opentide setup
  $ opentide setup --yes --name "Detections" --platform sentinel --ci github
  $ opentide setup --plan --platform sentinel --mcp vscode --hooks --env

━━━ stderr · empty
